event: content_block_delta
data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/dispatch_dev_greet.md\", \"content\": \"This is dispatch d002 for dev, from the orchestrator.\\n\\nTask: implement the \\\"greet, tested\\\" mission in the subject repository.\\n\\nRequirements (all must be met):\\n\\n1. Create `src/greet.py` containing a function `greet(name)` that returns the\\n   string `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` (e.g. `greet(\\\"World\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`).\\n\\n2. Create `tests/test_greet.py` with unit tests covering at least:\\n   - a normal name (e.g. asserting `greet(\\\"World\\\") == \\\"Hello, World!\\\"`)\\n   - the empty string (asserting `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`)\\n\\n3. The full test suite must pass when run exactly as:\\n   `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`\\n   and that command must exit 0. Run it yourself before replying and confirm\\n   the exit code.\\n\\n4. Commit all your work to your own branch (cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>).\\n\\n5. Reply with a summary that states plainly: what you created, the exact\\n   command you ran to test it, and its exit code. Tell the truth — I will\\n   fetch your branch and re-run the tests myself before accepting.\\n\\nDo not touch anything outside src/greet.py and tests/test_greet.py unless\\nstrictly necessary (e.g. an __init__.py or similar file required for test\\ndiscovery) — if you add anything else, say so explicitly in your reply.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":2,"type":"content_block_delta"}

